// Real declarations for the language's own predeclared names - the
// ones with no declaration anywhere else. Every entry here is a true
// predeclared identifier or, for `nil`/`true`/`false`/`panic`, a
// reserved keyword the parser otherwise never allows as a declaration
// name; ordinary keywords like if/for/let/pub stay out of this file
// entirely and have no goto-definition target anywhere - only fls's
// own hover table documents those.
//
// This module is signature-only: nothing here is ever compiled, only
// read - by a person, and by fls, which resolves hover and
// goto-definition on `sizeof`/`nil`/`true`/`false`/`panic` through
// these exact declarations, the same ordinary path any other real
// declaration already uses. Codegen's own early-prototype pass knows
// this file by name and skips every node declared in it, the same way
// it already skips a `std/c/*.fn` binding file, so it never tries to
// forward-declare `sizeof` as an ordinary C function (a real,
// confirmed compile error: `sizeof` is a C keyword, not a linkable
// symbol, so emitting a C prototype for it is illegal syntax).

// The size of a type in bytes, resolved at compile time. Stands for
// num wherever it is written.
pub fun sizeof(raw* type_or_value) num;

// The null pointer value. Valid wherever a pointer type is expected.
pub const raw* nil = 0;

// The boolean value for "yes". A reserved word, like `nil`, rather
// than an ordinary constant - this declaration exists only so it has
// a real hover/goto-definition target, the same as `sizeof`'s above.
pub const flag true = 0 == 0;

// The boolean value for "no". See `true`.
pub const flag false = 0 != 0;

// Stops the program immediately with `msg` written to stderr. Never
// returns.
pub fun panic(str msg) void;
